  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two immiscible liquids of refractive indices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> respectively are put in a beaker as shown in the figure. The height of each column is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. A coin is placed at the bottom of the beaker. For near normal vision, the apparent depth of the coin is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> is _______.</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0083_eabb1324027c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 247px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "31",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0083_eabb1324027c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 247px;\"/></p><p>The formula to calculate the apparent height of the coin when seen through the combination of liquids can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>app</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>app</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}